<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/001f935bb87b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "What the Eating Disorder Chatbot Disaster Tells Us About AI" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2926" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/03444bdc621d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "AI chatbot taken down after it gives ‘harmful advice’ on eating disorders" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2937" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/038524ee1a2c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On Monday, an activist named Sharon Maxwell posted on Instagram, sharing a review of her experience with Tessa." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2907" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/04bf79dd33a0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Eating disorder helpline shuts down AI chatbot that gave bad advice" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2906" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0a9846232b1c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The CEO clarified that the chatbot is not run by OpenAI's ChatGPT and is not a highly functional AI system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2936" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0ea8cbc34814> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Eating Disorder Association (NEDA) recently faced criticism and was compelled to take down its Tessa chatbot due to concerns that it was providing harmful and irrelevant information, as stated in an official social media post." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2931" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/109bc2964895> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Eating Disorder Helpline Disables Chatbot for ‘Harmful’ Responses After Firing Human Staff" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8242" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/12126fe97529> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Eating Disorders Association (NEDA) Helpline has disabled its brand-new chatbot, called Tessa, after two Instagram users posted that the chatbot recommended restricting calories, measuring skin folds, and other measures that can encourage disordered eating." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1419b2a1e5ee> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "If you want to set back the use of AI in mental health, start exactly this way and offend as many practitioners and potential users as possible, medical ethicist Art Caplan told Psychiatrist.com at the time." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2904" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1542ea2a6fb0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Eating Disorder Association (NEDA) received criticism and took down its AI chatbot Tessa after concerns arose that it provided harmful and irrelevant information, as stated in an official social media post." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2905" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/19f4006634f0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Crisis Text Line, a nonprofit that connects people to resources for a variety of mental health conditions, including eating disorders, anxiety, and more, is another place she says NEDA will refer people." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2942" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1caf4f151001> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The U.S. National Eating Disorder Association (NEDA) had implemented the chatbot named Tessa while subsequently announcing it would lay off all of its helpline’s human employees." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1e3660c34b93> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Abbie Harper, a member of the Helpline Associates United union and a hotline associate, noted in a blog post that the chatbot’s use takes away the personal aspect of the support system where staff can speak from their personal experiences." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2937" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/27fed653a9a5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "An Eating Disorder Chatbot Is Suspended for Giving Harmful Advice" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2903" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/291e03a3a571> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Eating disorder helpline that reportedly planned to fire its human staff disables its chatbot after a woman said it told her to count calories, weigh, and measure herself weekly" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2929" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2a71d1823e46> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NEDA announced Monday that it had suspended the chatbot, and the group’s CEO, Liz Thompson, says the organization is troubled by Tessa’s use of terminology that is “against our policies and core beliefs as an eating disorder organization.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2942" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2af449168567> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "She also says NEDA will direct people to the Crisis Text Line, a nonprofit that connects people to resources for a wide range of mental health issues, like eating disorders, anxiety, and more." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2903" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2b4dc86546c5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Eating Disorder Association (NEDA) has taken its chatbot called Tessa offline, two days before it was set to replace human associates who ran the organization’s hotline." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8242" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2b59f5ac9460> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Dr. Marzyeh Ghassemi, professor of machine learning and health at MIT, told NPR that if someone is disclosing an eating disorder, they probably don't want a generic link." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2901" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/31cec5806175> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Cass, maker of AI mental-health assistants, currently operates Tessa." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2898" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/32a997d9e62a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“With regard to the weight loss and calorie limiting feedback issued in a chat yesterday, we are concerned and are working with the technology team and the research team to investigate this further; that language is against our policies and core beliefs as an eating disorder organization,” Liz Thompson, the CEO of NEDA, told Motherboard in a statement." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2907" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/37c06a637c9f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Eating Disorder Helpline Takes Down Chatbot After It Promotes Disordered Eating" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2932" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/37efa43fe2ff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Abbie Harper, who was a hotline associate and member of the Helpline Associates United union, wrote in a blog post that the implementation of Tessa strips away the personal aspect of the support hotline, in which many associates speak from their personal experiences." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8242" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/38765d88a583> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The union has filed unfair labor practice charges with the National Labor Relations Board." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2902" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3e0b89c52553> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Responding to the Tessa backlash, NEDA CEO Liz Thompson told The Guardian that the organization is “concerned” and working with its technology and research teams to investigate the incidents further." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2901" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3f364c7e54e9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Katy Meta, a 20-year-old college student who has volunteered for the helpline, tells NPR, \"A lot of these individuals come on multiple times because they have no other outlet to talk with anybody...That's all they have, is the chat line.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2922" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/41d42c0ea85e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Dr. Ellen Fitzsimmons-Craft, a professor of psychiatry at Washington University’s medical school who helped design Tessa, told NPR." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2908" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/42a659bd2d4f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The nonprofit’s CEO Liz Thompson told Gizmodo:" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2909" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/462d235ace22> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2930] The National Eating Disorders Association has taken an AI chatbot offline for using “off-script” language and giving weight loss advice to those afflicted by eating disorders." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2930" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4845bd3edf16> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Abbie Harper – who as an NEDA associate helped launch Helpline Associates United (HAU), a union representing staff at the non-profit – alleged the decision to close the helpline, ditch its humans, and replace them with software was retaliation against their unionization." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2919" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/49c0d0f470a4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Dr. Marzyeh Ghassemi, Professor of Machine Learning and Health at MIT, told NPR that she didn’t think the chatbot could help callers the same way the volunteers and staffers did." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4a56ba5087fc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tessa, a program utilized by the National Eating Disorders Association, was discovered to be dispensing weight-loss and calorie-cutting recommendations that might make eating disorders worse." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2942" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4d316ddd9fd2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "An artificial intelligence chatbot named “Tessa” has been removed by the National Eating Disorder Association (NEDA) following accusations that it was giving harmful advice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2920" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4fab8819aa93> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In an email to Scripps News, NEDA CEO Elizabeth Thompson confirmed that they did find an underlying issue with Tessa but did not specify what the problem was." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2910" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/518f8706ab2f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"Every single thing Tessa suggested were things that led to the development of my eating disorder,\" wrote Sharon Maxwell, who describes herself as a weight inclusive consultant and fat activist, on Instagram." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2906" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/52c8cf8aec78> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NPR was informed by NEDA officials that the decision was unrelated to the unionization." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2920" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/58db3d8c0c23> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Woman Who Tested An Eating Disorder Helpline's AI Chatbot Says 'Every Single Thing' It Suggested Would Make Her Disorder Worse" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2943" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5aa0051fb353> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Less than 30 percent of people seek help from counselors, according to a Yale University study." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2903" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5ad0cfd96a49> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Non-Profit Helpline Shifts To Chatbots, Then Shuts Down Rogue AI" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2922" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5bf02d78410c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Problematic AI chatbot ‘Tessa’ that gave harmful eating disorder advice to shut down" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2931" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5c8de2a7e2c1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Eating disorder response chatbot taken offline following accusations of harm" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2934" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5d0ea3eff3ad> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NEDA pulls chatbot after users say it gave harmful dieting tips" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5dec0a549ace> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The problems with Tessa were made public by an activist named Sharon Maxwell, who said: “Every single thing Tessa suggested were things that led to the development of my eating disorder.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2908" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6025151a3fd9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Rauws did not respond to questions from WIRED about Tessa and the weight loss advice, nor about glitches in the chatbot’s responses." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2903" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/603710e993e7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Meta, for example, released a chatbot in August 2022 that openly blasted Facebook and made anti-Semitic remarks." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/60521c38770d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NEDA Suspends AI Chatbot for Giving Harmful Eating Disorder Advice" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2904" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/610381a00484> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When asked if Cass added any artificial-intelligence component to the bot, Cass Chief Executive Michiel Rauws said that the company uses AI to understand what users are typing and that some of its chatbots have generative AI, but he didn't say whether Tessa had generative features." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2898" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/645f37100533> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "An artificial intelligence chatbot named \"Tessa\" has been withdrawn by the National Eating Disorder Association (Neda) following accusations that it was giving harmful advice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2928" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/64a75915bcb3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Alexis Conason, a psychologist who specializes in treating eating disorders, was able to re-create the issues, posting screenshots of a conversation with the chatbot on Instagram." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2908" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/64ec658368a6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"It came to our attention last night that the current version of the Tessa Chatbot, running the Body Positive program, may have given information that was harmful and unrelated to the program,\" NEDA wrote on Instagram." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2938" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6ac2bf6bba18> a airo:Evidence ;
