<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/779a9ae066c4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NEDA announced on its Instagram page Tuesday it had taken down its Tessa chatbot after it “may have given information that was harmful and unrelated to the program.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2909" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7853d897d649> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Eating Disorder AI Chatbot Suspended After Telling People to Lose Weight" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2939" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/789bce1a41c4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "For example, UK energy supplier Octopus Energy’s CEO noted that AI has achieved higher customer satisfaction ratings than the company’s human employees." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2930" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7abc46bad286> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "They then filed for an election with the National Labor Relations Board and won on March 17, 2023." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7b33062b4522> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "National Eating Disorders Association Takes Down AI Chatbot After Users Say It Gave Dangerous Diet Tips" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2917" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7ca88f2c7cc1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Eating disorder AI chatbot disabled after giving out weight-loss advice - National" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2935" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7d013a599446> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2913] On March 31, the National Eating Disorders Association (NEDA), the largest nonprofit dedicated to eating disorders, decided to replace its human associates with the artificial intelligence (AI) chatbot Tessa tasked with providing support to people with eating disorders." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7d0553f764f7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Joanna Kandel, the founder and chief executive of the National Alliance for Eating Disorders, said the organization’s helpline received calls from people who were very upset by their interactions with Tessa, and she expressed concerns about outsourcing mental health care." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2900" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7dde993219e0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Group Replaces Hotline With Chatbot, Pulls Chatbot Over Bad Advice" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2916" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7df7d85803e9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "US-based NGO takes down AI chatbot on preventing eating disorders. Here's why" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2936" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8060ff5bd09f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Alexis Conason, a psychologist who specializes in treating eating disorders, also tried the chatbot out." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2907" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/81b8bf569ba0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Even though Tessa was built with guardrails, according to its creator Dr. Ellen Fitzsimmons-Craft of Washington University’s medical school." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2907" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8306d4d9d841> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2930] This was not how the chatbot was programmed, and X2AI/Cass' arrangement was to run the Body Positive program with zero opportunity for generative programming, NEDA CEO Elizabeth Thompson said in a comment to TheWrap, referring to the contracted company hired to launch the chatbot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2930" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8b0ee2e5036f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Thompson then quoted X2AI CEO Michiel Rauws as saying, “We are still trying to determine how a closed system allowed this type of content to be delivered.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2930" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8c410b75b0d0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2899] The bot, named Tessa, was the focus of social-media attention last week when users of the National Eating Disorder Association's website reported the rogue advice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2899" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8d71bc6eca3e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Wellness Chatbot Is Offline After Its ‘Harmful’ Focus on Weight Loss" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2900" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8dcb7f7ce0b6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Eating Disorder Association (Neda) has taken down an artificial intelligence chatbot, “Tessa”, after reports that the chatbot was providing harmful advice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2902" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8f2e15f21ad7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After sparking outrage, The National Eating Disorder Association reversed its decision to replace its Helpline staff members with an AI Chatbot named Tessa." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2943" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/90cd232023c0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The HAU, which has joined the Communications Workers of America Union, has now filed complaints alleging unfair labor practices with the NLRB, the US's workplace watchdog." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2919" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/93422151d53e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Eating Disorder Chatbot Taken Down After Giving Weight Loss Advice, Nonprofit Blames ‘Bad Actors’" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2930" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/963d4db57f9c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Liz Thompson, NEDA's CEO, says that delivering Body Positive is what Tessa was created to do." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2923" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/96b804348ca9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "And from the start, AI chatbots have been known to screw up. In one test chat with Microsoft's OpenAI-powered Bing chatbot, the software said it would like to steal nuclear codes." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2899" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/999922020ee6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NEDA's interim CEO Elizabeth Thompson reportedly decided to replace the association's human-operated helpline with the chatbot beginning June 1." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2919" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9de0edfb6a63> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Eating Disorders Association (NEDA) has disabled its chatbot Tessa two days before it'd have originally replaced the human associates who ran the hotline." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2938" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9e95651b6721> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It's a move that might delight anyone concerned about the potential job-killing effects from artificial intelligence tools. As the BBC reports, the US National Eating Disorder Association (NEDA) had to take down its AI chatbot \"Tessa\" after it began recommending potentially harmful diet strategies to people with eating disorders." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2916" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a44e427b9656> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Chatbot set to replace US eating disorder helpline pulled for pushing diets" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2933" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a8205328200a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Thompson also said the CEO of X2AI, the mental health artificial intelligence company that supports Tessa, reported that there was a “surge in traffic of 600% and behavior that indicated various forms of nefarious activity from bad actors trying to trick Tessa.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a9d8ba0a6be8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Daily Dot showed a screenshot from NEDA VP of communications and marketing Sarah Chase commenting on Maxwell’s post accusing her of promoting “a flat out lie.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2909" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aa9d86e6f369> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tessa is made available by the health technology business X2AI, currently known as Cass, which was established by businessman Michiel Rauws and provides text-based mental health counseling." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2942" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/acc1aec4fd2b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "‘This Robot Causes Harm’: Eating Disorder Helpline Forced To Ditch Chatbot That Made Eating Disorders Worse" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2941" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ae96d31c258e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to the report, NEDA worked with psycology researchers and AI company Cass AI which develops chatbots focusing on mental health." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2936" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b0dc8df6d3ac> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NYPD has been using Clearview AI's facial recognition technology since 2018." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2899" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b10d37e388e9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "National Eating Disorders Association takes its AI chatbot offline after complaints of ‘harmful’ advice" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b112370dd170> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The creator of Tessa says the chatbot, which was specifically designed for NEDA, isn’t as advanced as ChatGPT." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2908" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b19de4c5942b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Eating Disorders Association (NEDA) disabled its new helpline chatbot “Tessa” after it gave users with eating disorders advice about restricting calories and pinching their skin folds to measure fat." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2901" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b3de2be0725e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Ellen Fitzsimmons-Craft, an associate professor of psychiatry at Washington University School of Medicine, helped develop Tessa." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2898" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b77cc0fbe980> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Geoff Craddock, NEDA's board chair, can be heard telling associates: \"We will, subject to the terms of our legal responsibilities, \\[begin\\] to wind down the helpline as currently operating ... with a transition to Tessa, the AI-assisted technology expected around June 1.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2919" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b7f4e4501c19> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2898] The bot, named Tessa, operated on the website for the National Eating Disorders Association, and was meant to provide help for website users determined to be at risk for developing an eating disorder." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2898" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b9c9271dc65b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Dr. Ellen Fitzsimmons-Craft designed and developed the content to be 'an interactive eating disorder prevention program' while Cass — an evidence-based generative AI chat assistant within the mental health space — operated the chatbot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2923" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ba5595253812> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This was not how the chatbot was programmed, and X2AI/Cass' arrangement was to run the Body Positive program with zero opportunity for generative programming, NEDA CEO Elizabeth Thompson said in a comment to TheWrap, referring to the contracted company hired to launch the chatbot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2930" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bde0723a12de> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Dr. Ellen Fitzsimmons-Craft, a professor of psychiatry at Washington University’s medical school who helped design Tessa, told NPR." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2904" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c1d6e75c5d9b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Chatbot Was Designed to Help Prevent Eating Disorders. Then It Gave Dieting Tips." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2898" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c3339177b866> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Earlier this year, news outlet CNET was called out after it used an AI tool to generate stories that were riddled with errors, including one that offered some wildly inaccurate personal finance advice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c5f1f5ea5eb1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NEDA did not forgive Tessa’s mistake and terminated the AI chatbot after the backlash" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2920" .

