<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e6c1c0fe132d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On March 31, the National Eating Disorders Association (NEDA), the largest nonprofit dedicated to eating disorders, decided to replace its human associates with the artificial intelligence (AI) chatbot Tessa tasked with providing support to people with eating disorders." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e7aa92114fe1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Earlier this week, Sharon Maxwell and Alexis Conason each posted on Instagram about their experiences with the chatbot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2927" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e8e62e819964> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Eating Disorders Association has taken an AI chatbot offline for using “off-script” language and giving weight loss advice to those afflicted by eating disorders." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2930" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ea3876bcdde8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Chatbot intended to help people with eating disorders turns 'harmful'" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2910" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/eb25be6b337d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Turns Out Chatbots Aren’t Great at Eating-Disorder Counseling" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2901" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/eda901f3ea7b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The NEDA layoffs also came just days after the nonprofit’s small staff voted to unionize, according to a blog post from a member of the unit, the Helpline Associates United." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2903" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ef1e598f99bf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Eating Disorders Association Disabled Its Chatbot After It Gave Harmful Dieting Advice" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2927" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ef3c4bd2c7a8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NEDA's reliance on the chatbot stemmed from allegations that the organisation had terminated its human staff members when they attempted to unionise, as initially reported by Vice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2931" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f10aaa87132f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "— Rob Morris (@RobertRMorris) January 6, 2023" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2904" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f1741ebe272b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "I think there was some kind of error or bug in the system or a feature turned on that allowed some ChatGPT-like functionality in a program that was not designed to be that." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2910" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f3a247afb523> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Eating Disorder Helpline Takes Down Chatbot After Its Advice Goes Horribly Wrong" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2909" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f4e45b9d302b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In December, The New York Times reported that TikTok, Gen Z’s social media platform of choice, was suggesting video content encouraging and instructing the viewer on disordered eating within minutes of joining the platform as a new user." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2926" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f5a1ea08d359> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Then, in March the news outlet La Libre reported on a Belgian man who died by suicide after chatting with an AI chatbot on an app called Chai." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2904" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f5c6ef992ed1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lauren Smolar, VP at NEDA, says the increase in crisis calls also meant more legal liability." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2922" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f84c341bfeef> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Abbie Harper, in a blog post, criticized NEDA’s shift to AI, calling it a cover for union busting." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2905" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fbdbd6865faa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Neda worked with psychology researchers and Cass AI, a company that develops AI chatbots focused on mental health, to develop the chatbot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2902" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fe2e51c93e36> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Eating Disorder Chatbot Suspended for Harmful Advice" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2942" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fe74a28beb1b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "National Eating Disorder Association shuts down A.I. chatbot it planned to use to replaces humans saying it ‘may have given’ harmful information" ;
