<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/502b304a01db> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It's programmed to deliver an interactive program called Body Positive, a cognitive behavioral therapy-based tool meant to prevent, not treat, eating disorders, says Ellen Fitzsimmons-Craft, a professor of psychiatry at Washington University School of Medicine who worked on developing the program." ;
